DASH.glossary.hl={m:"Breadth",d:"New highs = NYSE stocks at a 52-week high; new lows = at a 52-week low. Index up while lows still dominate = a narrow bounce. Latest session (Wed 11 Nov): 45 highs vs 100 lows (WSJ), a little better than 47 vs 116 Tuesday, even though the S&P rose 1.31% — so the rally is still led by a few big AI names. Lows have beaten highs on every session in our chart this month except 4 Nov, so the base is still weak; more highs than lows again would be the next sign of healing."};

